WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.788 --> 00:00:06.230
Welcome to "Ear Biscuits", I'm Link.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.360
And I'm Rhett.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.470
This week, we're still at our

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:14.230
individual tables of adequate.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.830
I don't know if I've got
adequate lighting this week.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.840
We didn't think they were gonna be here.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.200
Hey, we're both wearing gray t-shirts

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.622
Is that better
Yeah, that's great.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.630
than being the same dimly lit round table?

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:27.490
That's our...
Funny thing is

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.760
is we're actually now in
contact with one another,

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.703
we shot GMM together.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.820
So we're no longer social
distancing from each other

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.000
because we basically have formed a pod

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.650
between our families and now with Stevie.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.523
But, here's the thing.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.750
We thought that we were
gonna be recording this

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.680
in the studio this week
and we are gonna be

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.710
shooting some GMM in the studio this week,

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.550
but there's a bunch of
construction going on

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.080
and people in and out of the studio.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.900
So in order to minimize
risk, we're in here again.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.470
So we lied, we're sorry.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:06.130
Oh no, we were mistaken.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:06.963
We were just wrong.

00:01:06.963 --> 00:01:09.270
We were mistaken, we were wrong,

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.103
But you know what?

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.250
We're more based up like this.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.743
Hopefully just this one.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:19.500
It is my birthday as we're recording this

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.290
as with everything else, nothing counts.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.413
I mean, you tweeted,

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:28.100
I appreciate you acknowledging
my birthday on Twitter.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.200
I will acknowledge that you
acknowledged my birthday

00:01:32.716 --> 00:01:33.549
right now.
There was a mild

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:35.790
acknowledgement given
the state of the world.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.040
I know, it's like,

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.910
we've been through so many milestones

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:43.090
here at my home like multiple birthdays,

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:48.010
multiple mother's day,
anniversaries, all types of stuff.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:51.453
And it's just so, it's so hard,

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:54.750
to work up the gumption to,

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:58.540
try to make it special because it's like,

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.587
you just feel like I'm just gonna wait.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:03.083
It'll be special again later.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:07.470
And so, I don't know, man.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:11.040
It's, and then you
compound, we're not just,

00:02:12.673 --> 00:02:15.663
we're not just living in
a world that's a pandemic.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.215
We're in crisis, here in America.

00:02:22.215 --> 00:02:23.430
Yeah, well,

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:24.323
so we'll talk about that
a little bit because

00:02:24.323 --> 00:02:28.660
what we're gonna talk
about when we get into the

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.580
main part of the episode is,

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.620
we're gonna be talking about getting older

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.590
and not just as two middle aged men

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.580
who are literally older now,

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:39.260
but just the process of growing
up and we're gonna touch

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.780
on some different stages in life.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.810
And we're using your
questions to explore that.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.050
Looking forward to that.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:47.478
Yeah, so whether you're
in your teens, your 20s,

00:02:47.478 --> 00:02:51.117
30s, 40s, wherever you are,

00:02:52.522 --> 00:02:55.680
we've, been through a lot of it

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.313
and we anticipate even more.

00:02:58.295 --> 00:03:00.500
So we'll be touching on
all that stuff hopefully.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.580
But before we get into that,

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:06.260
yes, we do want to acknowledge
what's going on in the world.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.870
I mean, last week, on "Ear Biscuits",

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:13.060
we were talking about that I wanted to,

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.480
because of just for my own personal health

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.130
to take a news break.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.670
Now wisely, you pointed out at the time

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.700
that was really a decision that was rooted

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.623
in my own privilege of being
able to just check out.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:29.227
And since then, and we
also, we talked about the,

00:03:29.227 --> 00:03:34.150
the murder of George Floyd
briefly and how that we had just

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.620
learned about that, when we
recorded the night before,

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.560
and I had a lot of anger about that.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:44.560
And just over the course
of the few days after that,

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:48.570
of course, protests broke
out throughout the nation.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.190
They're continuing to go on right now.

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:54.210
We've got curfews in place in
Los Angeles and things have

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.853
really gotten volatile out there.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.970
So we're not gonna do, I think

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:07.370
the thing that a lot of
times white folks like to do,

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.237
which is to be like,

00:04:08.237 --> 00:04:10.887
"Hey, let's get together
with other white folks

00:04:10.887 --> 00:04:13.100
"and talk about race."

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.700
I think that would be in one sentence,

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.420
that could be a little tone death.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:22.420
And I think that we
have made an effort to,

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.300
as a company, but also as individuals to,

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.210
say some things during this time,

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:30.160
but it's difficult...

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.990
One of the things that I've
learned just pretty recently

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:36.530
to be conscious about is just the idea

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:38.760
of not just doing the typical thing

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.510
where you kinda come in and say your piece

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:43.550
as if what you have to
say is super important.

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:46.370
I had a lot of things on
my mind and on my heart

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:48.880
about what was happening
and it hit me that

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:50.540
the most strategic thing that I could do

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:51.690
is just talk about a little bit

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:53.193
about what I've been learning,

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.043
especially from black voices who actually,

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:00.960
understand the history of
what's going on in our country

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.910
and understand why what's
happening right now is happening.

00:05:05.213 --> 00:05:09.970
And so instead of trying to
speak my mind necessarily,

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:13.670
what I did is I wrote a
letter to my former self

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:17.850
and tried to embody the way
that I used to think about

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.990
these issues which I was very
sure was a just and right

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.700
and logical way of thinking about them,

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.970
and I've since come to
the realization that

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:29.360
a lot of those thoughts
were based in my privilege,

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:33.140
in my whiteness, which is contrary to

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.570
what a lot of people on
the internet will say,

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:36.090
is not a myth.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.460
And I'll just jump in and say,

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:40.560
if you haven't read the Medium
article that Rhett wrote,

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.660
I'm super proud of the fact
that he put that down on paper

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.720
or you can watch him read it,

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:52.710
or listen to him read it
on his Instagram page.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:55.420
So here I am finally
promoting your Instagram.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.330
Well and also my Twitter,
so you can shout me out

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.700
on Twitter and Instagram

00:05:58.700 --> 00:05:59.739
Or Twitter.

00:05:59.739 --> 00:06:02.263
I decided to read it because,

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:05.650
we talked about this
last week as well I mean,

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:08.150
every once in a while
something gets me and I'm like,

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:11.210
I have to say something and
I'll write a Medium piece,

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.940
but it kinda just hit me,

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.140
a lot of people don't read, period.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.690
And a lot of people don't read,

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:19.643
Medium articles.
Take the time

00:06:19.643 --> 00:06:20.476
to just read an article.

00:06:20.476 --> 00:06:21.830
And a lot of people don't
wanna read something

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.900
from a guy who's famous on YouTube,

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.743
which I get that, neither do I.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:31.400
But I thought that by
taking the time to read it,

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.800
I could maybe communicate
how personal it was

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:36.380
and also get it out there.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:37.770
Because again, it's like,

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:42.770
I'm not trying to speak
into the culture at large,

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.910
and I'm not trying to be a voice

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:48.480
that is telling black people
how they should be acting

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:51.210
and reacting to what's going on.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:56.210
That's what a lot of white
people that I know like to do.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:00.050
But what I wanted to do, as I said,

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:02.450
the only thing that I'm an
authority on in this situation

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:04.460
is the way that I used
to think about this,

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:07.090
because I was there, it was me.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:11.180
And so, I just wanna talk about that.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:15.043
And so I'm not gonna rehash
it here, but like Links said,

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:21.600
that's what I have to
say about the situation.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:24.670
Of course, as a company, we're
doing what we can to support

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:28.650
the movement to fight racial
inequality and injustice,

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:32.143
both by speaking into
it, but also in giving.

00:07:33.566 --> 00:07:35.160
But I think, and instead of waiting until

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:36.840
the end of the episode to give a rec,

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.830
I wanna get my rec up
front because I think that,

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.570
rather than listen to us talk about it,

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:46.763
I'd like you to listen to a very,

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:50.880
very compelling black
voice on these issues.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:55.420
And one of the books that was
the most eyeopening for me,

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:58.870
was "Stamped From the
Beginning" by Ibram X. Kendi.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.533
So this is a, first of all,

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:04.060
thankfully he has two
versions of this book

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:06.557
because if you just read,
"Stamped From the Beginning",

00:08:07.641 --> 00:08:09.913
it's a long comprehensive book.

00:08:09.913 --> 00:08:12.450
It's a history book that covers

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:15.800
the history of racism
against black people,

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.800
starting even before America.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.820
But then the majority
of the book talks about

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:22.610
just the history of racism in America.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.860
Now if you're like us, if you're our age,

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:28.040
if you're from where we're from.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:30.950
I think we grew up kinda
just thinking that,

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:34.610
Yeah, of course there was
racism against black people.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:37.620
Back in the day, I mean, of
course there was slavery,

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:40.766
and then there was stuff before
the civil rights movement.

00:08:40.766 --> 00:08:43.580
But now, it's kinda like, I mean,

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.200
Hey, we had a black president.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.350
Everything's cool now, right?

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:52.120
And I think that's not
really understanding

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:57.120
the depth of racism in
America and what that means,

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.120
and what that has meant for
black people historically

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.520
and what that means for black people now.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:07.490
So I heavily, highly as
enthusiastically as possible

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:11.007
recommend reading or listening to

00:09:11.007 --> 00:09:12.577
"Stamped From The Beginning".

00:09:13.774 --> 00:09:17.180
And if that 19 and a
half hour audible book,

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:19.700
is a little bit too much
for you to bite off,

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.210
he actually collaborated with,

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:22.960
I think Jason Reynolds is his name.

00:09:25.178 --> 00:09:27.410
And did, I think it's
just called "Stamped".

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:31.070
And it's basically the teenage version of,

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.580
the content that's in
"Stamped From the Beginning".

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:35.120
It kinda changes the voice

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:38.080
and speaks a little bit in a less academic

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:41.040
and more like to speaking
to this generation.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:42.080
And it's a shorter read,

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:44.000
but it's essentially the same content.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.073
So, "Stamped" by Ibram X. Kendi.

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:50.040
Okay, I can get into that.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:54.250
Yeah, and I would just
say again the tendency,

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:56.950
and this has been my
tendency for my whole life.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:01.310
My tendency is just as
events unfold in the world

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:04.520
is to begin forming
opinions about those events,

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:08.030
and then beginning to
spout those opinions off

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:11.400
and talk to other people
about those opinions,

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:16.400
before listening and before
understanding the context.

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:23.630
And if you say things like
white privilege is a myth.

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:27.220
If you say that there
is no racist oppression

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:28.793
in America today,

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.420
A, you're flat wrong,

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.820
and the only way to
learn that you're wrong,

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:39.630
is to actually learn about the history

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:41.880
of racism and America.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:43.952
And you've gotta educate yourself,

00:10:43.952 --> 00:10:47.680
and that doesn't mean the US history class

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:49.540
that you took in high school did it,

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:52.370
because I took that same US history class,

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:54.320
and they didn't talk about this stuff.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.720
They didn't talk about
this stuff to the degree,

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:03.020
and with the accuracy and
the stepping out of the

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.190
traditional colonialist white perspective

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:07.717
in the way that Ibram is able to do,

00:11:07.717 --> 00:11:10.360
in "Stamped From the Beginning"
and also I recommend it

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:13.240
for other books that are kinda

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:15.990
come at things from a different
angle but are all great

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.270
in the Medium article that you can...

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:21.240
I recommend all those and
the rest of them are shorter,

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:22.530
if you wanna try one of those,

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.890
I've really had to come to grips with,

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:29.270
the fact that being on the
sidelines of this issue

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.663
is perpetuating the problem.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:35.780
There are a lot of quotes floating around

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:38.770
that are, say, much more
eloquently than that

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:40.083
but for me,

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:48.550
I haven't denied these problems

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:53.550
and I haven't sought to
actively undermine by any means.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:12:00.380
But I feel like I've been paralyzed,

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:05.380
because with a combination of
just not being educated enough

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:14.217
and having fear about
deciding to say or do things

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:20.043
because we're in this environment where,

00:12:20.043 --> 00:12:23.653
if you decide to say something,
my instinct is not to,

00:12:26.678 --> 00:12:29.460
take as little amount
of time as possible to

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.690
understand something just
so I can then turn around

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.040
and say where I stand on it.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:39.480
I'm very hesitant to take
stands on things because

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:43.140
I just don't have a lot of
confidence when it comes to

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:45.530
that type of thing.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:48.440
So instead, I just get intimidated,

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:50.854
and just kinda move on to the next thing.

00:12:50.854 --> 00:12:53.790
I'm troubled by it, but I'm kind of

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:58.340
frozen on the sidelines
and I've really come

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:02.653
to grips with like, I
don't wanna stay there.

00:13:07.203 --> 00:13:09.660
It's just acknowledging the
excuses in order to work through

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:14.030
them to say, hey, sometimes
if you say something

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:16.960
and you say the wrong thing,
even if you're trying to help,

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.340
then you make people upset
that you're trying to help

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:25.260
or if you put anything on the internet

00:13:27.469 --> 00:13:30.670
that shares something and that implies

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:32.830
that you're taking action or that

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.280
you believe other people
should also take action,

00:13:36.811 --> 00:13:38.133
it just puts a target.

00:13:39.195 --> 00:13:42.380
No matter what is being
said on the internet,

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.410
if you look underneath it,

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:48.803
most likely there someone
is very much opposed to it.

00:13:51.751 --> 00:13:55.293
And so I wig out trying to
anticipate what that is.

00:13:56.729 --> 00:13:58.650
It's paralyzing.

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:01.743
I find it really interesting
that one of the accusations,

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:05.880
one of the accusations
that we've received...

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:08.070
This year we become more vocal.

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:10.770
Obviously we've become more
vocal for a number of reasons.

00:14:10.770 --> 00:14:13.070
We became more vocal once we kind of

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:17.430
broke the story of our
de-conversion, deconstruction

00:14:18.855 --> 00:14:21.630
and people have perceived that we're

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.730
being more political or
talking about issues.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:25.970
I think that those things just happen to

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:29.480
coincide in one sense, but
it also coincided with 2020,

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:31.790
which is a year in which
you're not getting political.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.810
You're kind of missing the point.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:36.440
You're not participating if
you're not getting political.

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:40.320
But I'll say that one of the
accusations that we received

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:44.460
sorta multiple times is
"You guys are doing this

00:14:45.677 --> 00:14:48.887
"to please your audience."

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:52.810
Let me tell you everybody,

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:55.460
we've done nothing but lose audience.

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.860
We've done nothing but lose audience.

00:14:57.860 --> 00:14:59.210
Every time I tweet something

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:01.460
that is a little bit
controversial, I lose followers.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.790
So, we're not doing this to gain audience.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.870
I want as many people to
stick around as possible,

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:08.750
but that's not why we're doing it,

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:10.330
but to speak to what you're talking about

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:12.680
with this hesitation to say something

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.760
because you feel like you're
gonna say something wrong.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.880
First of all, you are going
to say something wrong.

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:18.750
When you speak into these things,

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:20.630
you are going to get it wrong.

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:23.210
And you don't mean that,
you're not singling me out.

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:24.517
I don't know, at this point.

00:15:24.517 --> 00:15:28.180
Anyone who makes a decision
to try to be a part of it

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:31.860
is gonna get it wrong and
it's just part of the process.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.950
But it's also the way that
we learn how to do it.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.370
And I think you'll be surprised that

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.300
if you just take a humble posture

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.030
and you take a posture that is like,

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:44.640
I'm here to learn, I'm here to listen.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.140
If I said that in the wrong way

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:48.390
or if I had an idea
that was actually based

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:51.770
in some cloak racism that I
didn't even know if I had,

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:54.430
point that out to me,
'cause I want to grow.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.610
And I think another aspect of that is

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:04.010
the more that I listen,
the more that I learn

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:08.753
the better way to engage.

00:16:08.753 --> 00:16:11.163
And this is a really recent thing for us.

00:16:13.512 --> 00:16:17.760
I think, the way that
I have thought and felt

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:21.209
about these issues of
racial injustice in America

00:16:21.209 --> 00:16:24.880
has been around for quite some time,

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:29.670
but the way that I'm actually
interacting and engaging

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:34.670
and sort of understanding
the depth of the problem,

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:38.820
the persistence of the problem.

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:40.340
That's something that's only come,

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:43.140
that's not gonna come by just
having a conversation with you

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:43.973
you know what I'm saying?

00:16:43.973 --> 00:16:46.890
Me and you can get together
and talk and pontificate

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:49.970
and philosophize about everything
until the cows come home

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:54.440
and we're never gonna
understand the situation

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:56.720
that's happening in black America.

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:58.070
The only way you're gonna understand that,

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:03.030
is you have to read,
listen to black voices.

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:04.620
And so if you're speaking into this,

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.700
but you haven't read a book

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.440
like "Stamped From the Beginning",

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:11.698
you haven't listened to a talk or a video,

00:17:11.698 --> 00:17:13.840
you're not following anybody on Twitter,

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:17.210
who's speaking from that perspective.

00:17:17.210 --> 00:17:19.972
You don't have the facts.

00:17:19.972 --> 00:17:24.972
You're coming into this with blinders on.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:28.260
And it took me a long time to...

00:17:28.260 --> 00:17:30.160
And that's not just the
case with this issue.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:32.020
That's the case with every issue.

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:33.860
It drives me crazy.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:36.353
The thing that drives me crazy is when,

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:40.333
if you find yourself in the wrong place,

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:45.760
on Twitter or scrolling
through the comments,

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.440
you get barraged,

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:51.810
you get pummeled by people who, there is,

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:55.990
I can discern no love or
empathy in their point of view.

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:59.520
It's one thing to disagree
or to make a counterpoint

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:02.010
or to come from a different place.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:07.010
But that's the one thing I
do feel like I can discern,

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:11.853
it's kind of sniff out,
like, is there any love,

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:15.340
any component of love
in what you're saying?

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:20.923
And, that's why it's
deeply disturbing to me.

00:18:22.124 --> 00:18:26.760
If I go to the president's
Twitter timeline,

00:18:30.895 --> 00:18:35.080
it deeply disturbs me that I cannot dis...

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:40.080
I cannot pick up just a grain
of empathy in what he says.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:45.480
I know we don't wanna...

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:47.890
It's like, well, here I am getting into...

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:50.650
Best, but hold on, but here's the thing.

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:54.130
That's not political,
that's just human intuition.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:55.940
I'm being honest with you.

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:59.550
Like seeing the fact that our country

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:02.100
is going through what it's
going through right now

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:05.420
and we have a president who

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:07.650
we don't even want him to speak about it

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:11.670
because him speaking
about it makes it worse.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:15.050
Like that's unprecedented
that we have a president

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:18.190
who we do not actually
want to say anything

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:20.040
because he will only inflame,

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:21.600
he will only divide.

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:24.650
That's not a political observation.

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:29.010
That's just a logical
observation about human behavior.

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:31.890
I don't care what side of
the spectrum you're on.

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:33.680
You cannot deny that fact.

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:36.670
He is not a leader, he is a divider.

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:38.730
He's making it worse.

00:19:38.730 --> 00:19:42.630
It's the absolute last thing
that we need right now.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:44.470
Hopefully it won't last much longer.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:49.423
So, let's shift to a broader
topic of getting older.

00:19:51.030 --> 00:19:55.030
But first, let's direct
you to the mythical store.

00:19:55.030 --> 00:19:57.200
mythical.com has all types of stuff.

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:58.627
Don't we just sell great t-shirts?

00:19:58.627 --> 00:20:02.490
'Cause that seems to be what
we're in the mood for today.

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:05.280
Well, great t-shirts in
all shapes and sizes.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:07.520
You got a V neck, it's kind of a baby V.

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:08.753
This was your shirt.

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:12.500
And somehow I got it and
now it's my favorite shirt.

